  "id": "confound",
  "term": "confound",
  "definition": "In this context, a confound is a source of distortion that makes a measure reflect something other than the psychological phenomenon it is meant to assess. The packet specifically describes a semantic confound, in which questionnaire scales may capture word-based familiarity or semantic associations instead of the underlying trait or state.",
